# Level 21 by password VXBB, the bubble gun, and then three levels finished in a
# row: 21 -> 22 -> 23 -> 24, arriving with the weapon still in inventory slot 2.
#
# This is the movie the last six rounds of route arithmetic were for. `$81:983A`
# stands at (239,715) on record 25 and no record places both it and a gun, so the
# creature has to be met carrying one collected earlier. It had never been shown
# that a weapon survives *any* level transition. It survives three.
#
#   1885  level 21, `$1D50` = `$0001` -- VXBB is variant 1, one neighbour
#   3643  the bubble gun. `$7E:1CD0` = `$0040`
#   4238  rescue     4604  exit      5026  level 22
#   5866  door one   6078  door two
#   6897  rescue     7442  exit      7864  level 23
#   9197  rescue     9443  exit      9833  level 24, `$7E:1CD0` still `$0040`
#
# **The gun costs eight frames.** The climb up level 21's x=504 column passes
# (504,1340) at frame 3635 and the type `$04` object is at (485,1340), nineteen
# pixels west on a row the route already crosses. `movies/level21-bubble.zmv`
# spends a whole climb on the same weapon.
#
# **Level 22 spawns the player in a locked yard.** The record says (541,1095);
# the walls read `$0053`, which is attribute bit 6, which is a door (`$80:B0BB`),
# and the two `$08` objects in the yard are keys (`$80:CA30`: type `$08` -> id
# `$21`). `zamn_assets route` called the level impossible until it learned the
# bit; `route --doors` plans it in 239 cells.
#
#   5660  key at (299,1094), straight off the walk west
#   5763  key at (290,1079), eight frames of Up
#   5866  door at (461,1070). `$1D0C` 2 -> 1 and one 8x8-tile block is gone
#   6078  door at (365,830).  `$1D0C` 1 -> 0
#
# The two pushes are hand-written and have to be: opening a door is a leg held
# into a wall, which is what `fit_route.py`'s stall guard exists to abandon.
# `--doors` plans the far side; fit up to the doorway, cut the movie at the
# *arrival* frame, push by hand, restart the loop.
#
# **An exit door needs somewhere to go.** `$82:F7D2` tries eight offsets around
# the player and takes the first `$80:AE14` accepts. Level 22's rescue finishes
# at (567,137) in a two-tile corridor under the top of the map, and all eight are
# refused -- no door, for seven hundred frames, with both of `$80:8544`'s
# conditions already true. Walking 238 pixels west to (329,137) puts one at
# (439,169). The step onto it releases Right at 7255 and not 7257: x=439 is the
# open column and x=443 is four pixels into a wall.
#
# Level 23 wanted none of that. Thirty fitted legs from its own declared spawn
# (403,508) to the victim at (887,526), and its exit door spawns at (911,556) --
# thirty-six pixels directly below the player, which is what the same eight-offset
# search looks like when there is room around it.
#
# Level 24 loads at (50,81) with the gate at `$0001`. The creature is at
# (239,715), the walk to it is 80 cells with 38 of them inside doors, and the
# level carries nine `$08` keys. That leg is not in this movie yet.
